4) Capabilities card compact layout and dismiss
- Action: On empty chat, inspect capabilities card.
- Result: Card uses reduced padding, smaller logo (h-10 w-10), tightened typography.
- Observed: "Skip intro" button present in top-right.
- Action: Attempt to click "Skip intro" via Playwright.
- Result (before fix): First attempt was blocked when the session selector modal was open (overlay intercepting pointer events). After closing the modal and retrying, Next.js dev overlay reported a client-side error: "Rendered fewer hooks than expected" referencing the Chat component.
- Fix: Moved the Skip intro state up into `Chat` (using `showCapabilitiesCard`), and changed `CapabilitiesCard` to be a pure presentational component with an `onSkipIntro` callback (no internal hooks besides `useMemo`).
- Result (after fix): With the modal closed, clicking "Skip intro" hides the capabilities card and leaves the chat area with pills + input only. No runtime error is raised.
- Status: PASS (post-fix)

